        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Polynomials and Fields",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FINITE FIELDS:\n  F_{p^n} = GF(p^n) exists and is UNIQUE (up to isomorphism) for every prime p and n≥1.\n  |F_{p^n}| = p^n.\n  (F_{p^n})* is cyclic of order p^n - 1 (primitive element theorem).\n  Subfields: F_{p^m} ⊆ F_{p^n} iff m | n.\n  F_{p^n} ≅ F_p[x]/(f) for any irreducible f of degree n over F_p.\n```"
    },
