        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[polynomials, fields]",
        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Polynomials and Fields",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FACTORIZATION BY DEGREE:\n  Over C (algebraically closed): every f = product of linear factors.\n  Over R: every f = product of linear and irreducible quadratic factors.\n  Over Q: factorization can be complicated; irreducible polynomials of any degree exist.\n  Over F_p: every element of F_p is a root of x^p - x; x^{p^n}-x = product of\n    all monic irreducibles of degree dividing n over F_p.\n```"
    }
